      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The use of metoprolol combined with nifedipine and diltiazem was studied and compared in 32 patients suffering from coronary disease associated with angina pectoris of effort. The drug combinations indicated appeared equally effective in patients with angina pectoris, functional class III. In patients with angina pectoris of effort, functional classes III-IV, the combined use of metoprolol and diltiazem turned out superior as compared with nifedipine which is related to different hemodynamic effects of the drugs."},
